<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly softer.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly softer.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were mostly softer on Friday, with only the one-week and one-year rates anchored at the same level, traders said.</p>
<p>Dealers said the closure again of the Central Bank's overnight borrowing facility made the system more liquid and prodded banks to adjust their swap rates.</p>
<p>PHIBOR represents rates at which banks would be willing to swap their pesos for dollars.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  MARCH 21		 MARCH 20</p>
<p>    1 W		8  5/8		  8  5/8</p>
<p>    2 W		8  9/16		 8  5/8</p>
<p>    1 M		8 11/16		 8  3/4</p>
<p>    2 M		8  3/4		  8  7/8</p>
<p>    3 M		8 13/16		 8  7/8</p>
<p>    6 M		9  1/16		 9  1/8</p>
<p>    12M		9  1/2		  9  1/2</p>
<p>    VAL		24-Mar		  21-Mar</p>
<p>--LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
